{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And he split wood for a burnt offering</b> — His alacrity in the commandment. Perhaps no wood would be found there in that place, so he carried it for three days. Or perhaps Abraham would disqualify for an offering any wood in which a worm was found, according to the law of the Torah (Middot 2:5), and so he took from his house good wood for a burnt offering. And thus Scripture says, \"and he split wood for a burnt offering.\""], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:33:10.259649574Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}